\title{CAPmethods: Covariate-Assisted Principal (CAP) Regression Methods}
\description{
A unified collection of covariate-assisted principal (CAP) regression methods for relating subject-level covariates to the covariance/heterogeneity structure of multivariate and longitudinal outcomes. Includes high-dimensional CAP (HDCAP; with optional covariance shrinkage, which also covers the classical CAP model when shrinkage is disabled), longitudinal CAP with a time-invariant projection (LCAP), multilevel CAP with cluster-varying loadings (MCAP), covariance-on- covariance regression (CAP-CoC), CAP mediation, high-dimensional-covariance CAP (HDcov/HCAP), and CAP clustering. Computational kernels are implemented in C++ via 'RcppArmadillo'.
